"""Product help grounded in the actual local portal, rather than general banking advice."""
PORTAL_HELP = [
    {"id":"NG-PORTAL-13","title":"Connecting Gemini or another chat app with read-only access","keywords":"connected apps connections gemini mcp oauth account link disconnect revoke read only personal chat integration","text":"Open Connected Apps in the left navigation. Copy the read-only connection address into a compatible MCP chat app, then sign into Northgate and choose Allow read-only access. No shared API key is needed. The connection can list the portal's shared synthetic cases, inspect received/missing document checklists and read existing drafts. It cannot generate, edit, discard, approve, send or change settings. Cases are not individually assigned. Under Your connections choose Disconnect to revoke access immediately. Connections expire after 30 days. Personal Gemini setup is Settings > Connected Apps > Add a custom app; Google currently documents US users aged 18+, English and Keep Activity enabled. Google controls availability. Gemini requires a public HTTPS address; localhost is for local testing."},
    {"id":"NG-PORTAL-01","title":"Finding cases and moving between pages","keywords":"queue cases search company filters jurisdiction city pagination pages previous next six 6 42","text":"Choose Case Queue in the left navigation. The prototype contains 42 fictional companies. Each page shows up to six cases. Use Previous, numbered pages 1–7, and Next at the bottom of the results box. Search by company name or case reference, filter by London, Singapore or New York, or select nudges due. Changing a filter returns you to page 1. Open a case with Review & chase or Review nudge."},
    {"id":"NG-PORTAL-02","title":"Choosing Auto-draft or Guided draft","keywords":"auto automatic guided manual mode setting toggle top bar header audio drafting preference","text":"The Auto-draft / Guided draft selector is in the top bar immediately before Audio. The choice applies across the workspace and is remembered in your browser, including other tabs. Auto-draft prepares and checks an email automatically when a case needs a draft; an existing passing review draft can be reused. Guided draft starts with no prepared email and waits for your instructions and the Draft button. Both modes require RM approval before sending. The mode selector is disabled while a currently observed run is working."},
    {"id":"NG-PORTAL-03","title":"Giving drafting or redrafting instructions","keywords":"instruction guidance prompt write style email concise tone redraft rewrite revise optional empty mandatory five 5","text":"Open Gap Workspace and the AI workflow view. The drafting/redrafting guidance text box is below the workflow animation in both modes. In Guided draft enter at least five non-whitespace characters, then choose Draft. In Auto-draft guidance is optional: leave it empty for the default style, or add wording, formality, length or emphasis instructions before choosing Redraft. These instructions are passed to the agents for the next draft and cannot override missing-document checks, QA or RM approval. The box is disabled during generation."},
    {"id":"NG-PORTAL-04","title":"Using the Gap Workspace and live AI workflow","keywords":"gap workspace workflow graph animation diagram drafter flip stream live activity steps agents received locked missing progress","text":"In Gap Workspace, the left pane shows received documents locked from chasing and the missing-document checklist. The right pane flips between Drafter and AI workflow. Guided draft initially opens AI workflow so you can see the process before starting. The workflow shows Document check → Orchestrator → Drafter → Toner → Critique QA; the live activity feed reports actual actions and revisions. Drafter shows live unreviewed wording during generation. You can change views or navigate away while a run continues; returning reconnects to its events. Only the final QA-passing draft is eligible for RM review."},
    {"id":"NG-PORTAL-05","title":"Reviewing, editing, approving or discarding a draft","keywords":"review edit save approve send discard reject gate scorecard blocked received document stale","text":"After generation, open Drafter in Gap Workspace. Read the subject, body and QA scorecard. RMs or admins can edit and choose Save edits & recheck QA. Unsaved edits or failed QA keep Approve & Send disabled. Approve & Send checks the current document store again and records a message in the synthetic outbox; this prototype sends no external client email. Discard requires a reason. A newly received document can make an older draft stale, so read the checklist and redraft. Neither drafting mode approves a send automatically."},
    {"id":"NG-PORTAL-06","title":"Inspecting Agent Trace","keywords":"trace traces agent history ledger audit evidence inspect all agents read only readonly","text":"Choose Agent Trace to inspect recorded activity for Document check, Orchestrator, Drafter, Toner, Critique QA and Portal Guide. This page is read-only: it has no Draft or Redraft controls. Use the case and agent filters to narrow the execution ledger and select an event to open its evidence drawer. All agents are shown by default, including portal conversations that have no case ID. The latest 200 matching case events are retrieved and the view refreshes every three seconds. Start new drafting work in Gap Workspace."},
    {"id":"NG-PORTAL-07","title":"Managing three-day follow-ups","keywords":"nudge follow up followup days three 3 overdue reply response tracker awaiting","text":"Choose 3-Day Nudges to view Due now, Awaiting reply and Replied. When a chase has no recorded reply after three calendar days, the worker flags it for review; it never sends automatically. Review nudge opens the case workspace. RMs, analysts or admins can Record client reply to suppress future nudges for that outreach. Generate and review a nudge using the same RM approval gate."},
    {"id":"NG-PORTAL-08","title":"Changing voice and prompts in Toner Studio","keywords":"toner studio prompt formality urgency jurisdiction version golden regression admin settings tone","text":"Toner Studio lets an admin edit Orchestrator, Drafter, Toner and Critique prompts, adjust formality, urgency and jurisdiction wording, and run the five-case golden-set regression. Save version becomes available only after the exact candidate settings pass the test. Other roles can inspect the studio but cannot publish prompt changes. For a one-off wording request use the drafting/redrafting instructions in Gap Workspace instead of changing system prompts."},
    {"id":"NG-PORTAL-09","title":"Understanding FinOps and provider availability","keywords":"finops costs tokens spend latency model provider gemini groq failover outage roi savings dashboard","text":"FinOps & Impact shows recorded agent token usage, estimated USD/GBP cost, per-case costs, latency, provider attempts, successful failovers and RM discard rate. The 3,000 case-days per month figure is a projection, not a measured outcome. Admins can use Simulate Gemini outage to test Groq recovery. When a provider fails, inspect the error or Agent Trace and retry later; only an admin should change server API configuration. API keys are never shown in the browser."},
    {"id":"NG-PORTAL-10","title":"Using Portal Guide, Clear and Back","keywords":"portal guide help chatbot chat clear back question sources navigation use portal","text":"Portal Guide primarily explains how to use this Northgate prototype, its screens, buttons and workflows. Choose a starting question or enter your own question and press Enter or the send arrow. View sources expands supporting product-help or policy references. Clear chat removes messages, the current question and any error, and cancels a pending answer. The small X clears only the typed question. Back returns to the Portal Guide welcome screen, clears the current conversation and cancels any pending answer; it does not leave Portal Guide. The guide answers questions; it does not click buttons or change cases for you."},
    {"id":"NG-PORTAL-11","title":"Controlling appearance and interface sounds","keywords":"audio sound mute off on dark light theme sun moon animation motion top bar","text":"The top bar contains drafting mode, Audio and Dark / Light in that order. Select Audio to turn optional interface sounds on or off; it starts off and remembers your choice. Sounds occur after user interaction for navigation, stage handoffs, revisions and completion, with no background music. Select Dark / Light to switch appearance using the moon/sun toggle. The interface respects the browser or operating system reduced-motion setting."},
    {"id":"NG-PORTAL-12","title":"Operator roles and available controls","keywords":"role permissions login rm analyst coo admin disabled account sign in","text":"The demo login offers RM, analyst, COO and admin roles. Analysts can generate drafts and record synthetic document receipts; RMs and admins review, edit, approve or discard drafts. COO is read-only. Only admins can publish system prompts or simulate provider outages. If a button is disabled, check your role, whether a run is active, whether guided instructions have five characters, whether edits are saved, and whether QA passed. All case data and outreach in this prototype are synthetic."},
]
